; circles_conv is a training integration run on the `train` tier (see the aggregate above): it
; and fsm_transformer/transformer_names are the heaviest members of the serialized
; `ocannl_training_test` chain on every substrate measured (~95s on a 24-thread Linux box, ~129s
; on the reference Mac), so in the default suite they set CI's wall-clock tail. The loss
; accumulates on device (Train.grad_update ?accum_loss) so the loop syncs once per epoch; its sgd
; step is autotuned (materialized intermediates + Autotune.tune). NOTE: ~87s on cc, ~76s on
; the metal backend with a cold tune search on the reference Mac (batch 32 / 3.75k steps: the
; remaining metal cost is compilation plus GPU execution of the fissioned step's ~40 serialized
; dispatches).

(executable
 (name circles_conv)
 (modules circles_conv)
 (libraries ocannl dataprep arrayjit.verdict training_golden)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_here ppx_ocannl)))

